Nhưng mà em khuyên mọi người thì càng đơn giản là càng tốt nha mọi người.

390
00:16:18,050 --> 00:16:19,990
Đấy, chứ đừng có quá là màu mè nha

391
00:16:19,990 --> 00:16:21,710
Khán giả họ thì không thích đâu

392
00:16:21,710 --> 00:16:24,970
Rồi, bây giờ thì mình sẽ thêm một tí hiệu ứng chuyển cảnh nữa nha mọi người

393
00:16:24,970 --> 00:16:28,370
Để cho video mình nó thêm sinh động và linh hoạt hơn nha

394
00:16:28,370 --> 00:16:30,350
Như vậy là xong rồi đó mọi người ạ

395
00:16:30,350 --> 00:16:32,790
Toàn bộ phần edit là đã xong rồi nha

396
00:16:32,790 --> 00:16:35,500
Thì bây giờ em sẽ cho mọi người xem qua cái demo mà em vừa tạo ra nha.

397
00:16:36,000 --> 00:16:40,500
There's a peculiar thing about human life.

398
00:16:40,500 --> 00:16:42,500
We are always, in some sense, trying to get somewhere,

399
00:16:43,100 --> 00:16:44,700
to be something more than we are,

400
00:16:44,800 --> 00:16:49,000
to become successful, enlightened, wise, pure, peaceful,

401
00:16:49,000 --> 00:16:52,600
or, perhaps most ironically, to become ourselves.

402
00:16:53,200 --> 00:16:56,200
But all this striving, all this endless becoming,

403
00:16:56,200 --> 00:16:59,500
hides a simple truth that you already are,

404
00:16:59,500 --> 00:17:02,800
and the more you chase being, the more it slips away.

405
00:17:03,200 --> 00:17:06,900
It's rather like trying to smooth out a pond's surface by hand.

406
00:17:07,100 --> 00:17:09,500
The moment you touch it, you only make more ripples,

407
00:17:09,500 --> 00:17:11,600
and so it is with the self.

408
00:17:11,900 --> 00:17:15,300
The harder you try to be yourself, the less you are.

409
00:17:15,800 --> 00:17:19,900
You see, there is a kind of fundamental mischief in our minds.

410
00:17:21,200 --> 00:17:25,300
We are taught from the very beginning that life is a sort of race,

411
00:17:26,200 --> 00:17:29,100
that you must plan, predict and perfect.

412
00:17:30,100 --> 00:17:32,500
And somewhere, if you keep working at it,

413
00:17:32,800 --> 00:17:36,000
if you keep thinking about it, you'll arrive. At what? At yourself.

414
00:17:39,000 --> 00:17:42,000
But of course, you never quite get there.

415
00:17:43,100 --> 00:17:46,700
Because the self you seek is always one thought ahead,

416
00:17:47,900 --> 00:17:49,200
one breath away,

417
00:17:50,200 --> 00:17:52,400
one goal further down the line.

418
00:17:53,700 --> 00:17:55,000
It's a mirage.

419
00:17:56,200 --> 00:18:02,700
A carrot dangling before the donkey, who doesn't realise he's the one holding the stick.

420
00:18:03,000 --> 00:18:03,420
Now!
